### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. ________

ENTITLED:
"A RESOLUTION SUPPORTING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE’S
APPLICATION FOR A LAND AND WATER CONSERVATION FUND
GRANT FOR THE MARTIN LUTHER KING JR. PARK TENNIS
COURT REMOVAL AND RECLAMATION PROJECT."

WHEREAS, the single tennis court at Martin Luther King Jr. Park is deteriorated beyond repair, does not
meet current tennis play standards, has become a neighborhood eyesore and a safety hazard; and

WHEREAS, the Parks & Recreation Department proposes to remove the tennis court and reclaim the area
as open, landscaped park space that is consistent with and integrated into the park; and

WHEREAS, the cost for the removal and reclamation is estimated to be $56,000; and

WHEREAS, a grant in the amount of $28,000 is being requested from the Land and Water Conservation
Fund; and

WHEREAS, the Martin Luther King Jr. Park Tennis Court Removal and Reclamation Project is an
eligible project to receive a Land and Water Conservation Fund Grant and the required local match will
come from “in-kind”, valued at $17,225 and 5th Penny Sales Tax (2007-2010) funds estimated at $10,775.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING:

That the City of Cheyenne Governing Body supports a Land & Water Conservation Fund Grant application
for the Martin Luther King Jr. Park Tennis Court Removal and Reclamation Project and that the City will
provide the required match for the grant.

 That the Mayor of the City of Cheyenne, or other City official designated by the Mayor, is authorized to
sign an application for a LWCF grant for a corner rehab project in Martin Luther King Jr. (MLK) Park.
Further, that the Mayor is authorized to execute a grant agreement, in the event grant funds are awarded to
the City of Cheyenne for the MLK Tennis Court Removal and Reclamation Project.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS_________ DAY OF December, 2010.

___________________________
Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor

(Seal)

ATTEST:

__________________________________
   Carol A. Intlekofer, City Clerk

X: L&WCF Grants:L&WCF 11 Res Reclaim Corner.docx
```

